  "Question": "When an ellipse is used to describe a planet's orbit, where is the Sun usually placed?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "At an endpoint of the major axis",
    "B": "At an endpoint of the minor axis",
    "C": "Outside the ellipse",
    "D": "At one focus"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "This is a common application of the definition of an ellipse: the sum of the distances to the two foci is constant, and the Sun is at one of the foci.",
